## HATEOAS (Hypermedia Links)

We embed links in responses so clients can discover and navigate the API ([reference](https://code-maze.com/hateoas-aspnet-core-web-api/)).

### Link Model

Use `HateoasLink` from `MyPcBuild.ApiService.Infrastructure`:

```csharp
public record HateoasLink(Uri Href, string Rel, HttpMethod Method);
```

### Link Generation

```csharp
using MyPcBuild.ApiService.Infrastructure;

string baseUrl = httpContextAccessor.GetBaseUrl();

List<HateoasLink> links =
[
    new HateoasLink(new Uri($"{baseUrl}/api/catalog/products/{id}"), "self", Infrastructure.HttpMethod.GET),
    new HateoasLink(new Uri($"{baseUrl}/api/catalog/products"), "all-products", Infrastructure.HttpMethod.GET)
];
```

> Use `Infrastructure.HttpMethod` (not `System.Net.Http.HttpMethod`) for the enum.

### Conventions

| Rel value     | Meaning                              | Example |
|---------------|--------------------------------------|---------|
| `self`        | Current resource                     | GET same URI |
| `next` / `prev` | Pagination                         | Paginated list links |
| `category`    | Related category filter              | Products by category |
| `product`     | Link to product detail               | Nested product in build |
| `add-part`    | Add a part to a build                | POST to builds/{id}/parts |
| `remove`      | Remove a part                        | DELETE part |
| `validate`    | Validation endpoint                  | Compatibility/spatial validate |
| `catalog`     | Product catalog                      | GET /api/catalog/products |
| `create-product` | Create a product                 | POST /api/catalog/products |

### Response Shape

- **Single resource**: Response record with `Links` property (e.g. `GetProductByIdResponse`).
- **Collection**: Top-level `Links` + each item has its own `Links` (e.g. `GetProductsResponse`, `ProductSummary`).
- **Nested resources**: Include `Links` on nested DTOs (e.g. `ProductDetails` in build response).

### Base URL

Inject `IHttpContextAccessor` and use `httpContextAccessor.GetBaseUrl()` for all `Href` values. Never hardcode host or port.

---

## Checklist for New Endpoints

1. Add `{EndpointName}.cs` under `{Feature}/Endpoints/`.
2. Define Request and Response records (Response includes `List<HateoasLink> Links`).
3. Register in `{Feature}Endpoints.cs` via `app.Map{EndpointName}Endpoint()`.
4. Include `self` link; add contextual links (e.g. `product`, `category`, `add-part`).
5. Use `.WithName()` and `.WithTags()` for OpenAPI and routing.
